# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command scrape
shell rust
usage 1   scrape ls [<choice>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos]
usage 2                                 the chosen games, one a line: path, system, and where each kind comes from
usage 3   scrape plan [<choice>...] [<option>...]
usage 4                                 what a run would ask: games, requests, the day's quota left; nothing is sent
usage 5   scrape run [<choice>...] [<option>...] [--resume]
usage 6                                 the plan on standard error, then the run: one line a game as it finishes
usage 7   scrape status                 the quota, the account and the run going, one key a line
usage 8   scrape wait [scrape<n>]       follow a run that went on in the background (ps lists it, kill stops it)
usage 9   choices: --system <s>, --favorites, --collection <name>, --missing <kind>|any, <path>..., or paths on stdin
usage 10   options: --kinds, --videos, --overwrite, --region <r>, --language <l>, --threads <n>

case the usage, and what a command line refuses
target none
covers 1-10
$ scrape
out 368
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
action none
$ scrape frobnicate
out 368
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
action none
$ scrape ls --overwrite
out 418
scrape: --overwrite is not an option of scrape ls
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
action none
$ scrape plan --kinds boxart
out 165
scrape: --kinds boxart: not a kind; the kinds are cover, screenshot, marquee, titlescreen, miximage, backcover, 3dbox, physicalmedia, fanart, manual, video, or theme
status 1
action none
$ scrape plan --missing wheel
out 164
scrape: --missing wheel: not a kind; the kinds are cover, screenshot, marquee, titlescreen, miximage, backcover, 3dbox, physicalmedia, fanart, manual, video, or any
status 1
action none
$ scrape run --resume --system snes
out 465
scrape run --resume: an interrupted run goes on as it was queued, so it takes no choice or kinds
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
action none
$ scrape plan --threads 0
out 409
scrape: --threads needs a number above 0
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
action none
$ scrape plan --system
out 399
scrape: --system needs a value
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
action none
$ scrape status now
out 401
scrape status takes nothing more
Usage: scrape ls|plan|run [--system <s>] [--favorites] [--collection <name>] [--missing <kind>|any] [<path>...] [--kinds <k,...>|theme] [--videos] [--overwrite] [--region <r>] [--language <l>] [--threads <n>] [--resume] | scrape status | scrape wait [scrape<n>]
  Paths on standard input, one a line (the first tab-separated field), are chosen by hand. See man scrape.
status 1
